  "full_response": "**Policy Document: Handling Internal Only Documents**\n\n**Purpose:**\nThis policy outlines the procedures and responsibilities for employees regarding the handling of documents labeled as \"INTERNAL_ONLY.\" These documents contain sensitive information intended solely for internal use and must be protected to maintain confidentiality and comply with organizational standards and legal requirements.\n\n**Scope:**\nThis policy applies to all employees and contractors who access, handle, or distribute INTERNAL_ONLY documents.\n\n**Definitions:**\n\n- **INTERNAL_ONLY Documents:** Documents explicitly marked with the label \"INTERNAL_ONLY.\" These documents contain sensitive or proprietary information not meant for external dissemination or unauthorized internal distribution.\n\n**Policy Guidelines:**\n\n1. **Identification and Access:**\n   - Employees are responsible for identifying documents labeled as INTERNAL_ONLY. Access to such documents should be restricted to authorized personnel only, based on their need-to-know and job responsibilities.\n   - Ensure that access control measures, such as passwords or security permissions, are in place when storing or sharing INTERNAL_ONLY documents electronically.\n\n2. **Handling and Storage:**\n   - INTERNAL_ONLY documents should be stored securely, both physically and electronically. \n   - Use encrypted storage solutions for digital files and locked cabinets or safes for physical copies.\n   - Do not leave INTERNAL_ONLY documents unattended. Secure them when exiting an area, even for short periods.\n\n3. **Distributing and Sharing:**\n   - Sharing of INTERNAL_ONLY documents should be conducted only within approved channels and with authorized individuals who require access for legitimate business purposes.\n   - Use secure, approved systems for transferring documents electronically. Do not send INTERNAL_ONLY documents via unsecured email or personal devices.\n\n4. **Printing and Disposal:**\n   - When printing INTERNAL_ONLY documents, ensure they are kept secure if left unattended and disposed of according to confidentiality guidelines.\n   - Shred or otherwise securely destroy INTERNAL_ONLY documents that are no longer needed to prevent unauthorized access.\n\n5. **Incident Reporting:**\n   - Report any suspected or actual breaches of INTERNAL_ONLY document security immediately to the designated compliance officer or security team.\n   - Maintain a log of all incidents involving INTERNAL_ONLY documents, including actions taken to address the issue.\n\n6. **Training and Awareness:**\n   - Employees must complete training on document security protocols, including the proper handling of INTERNAL_ONLY documents, as part of their onboarding process and periodically thereafter.\n   - Stay informed of updates to this policy and related procedures.\n\n**Compliance and Enforcement:**\nFailure to comply with this policy may result in disciplinary action, up to and including termination of employment or legal consequences, depending",
